<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>CorpAPI — Dashboard</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/lab.css">
</head>
<body data-theme="api">
<div class="lab-topbar"><a class="lab-back" href="/challenges">&larr; ZeroDay Academy</a><span class="name">CorpAPI</span><span class="tag">/labs/cors-wildcard-credentials</span></div>
<div class="lab-wrap">
  <div class="lab-card">
    <h1>API Dashboard</h1>
    <p>Your API key (partial): <strong><%= apiKeyPreview %></strong></p>
    <p>Access your full API key via the authenticated API endpoint. The service reflects any <code>Origin</code> and allows credentials.</p>
    <p><a class="lab-link" href="/labs/cors-wildcard-credentials/api/secret" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Call /api/secret from this origin</a></p>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-card">
    <h2>Cross-origin attack simulation</h2>
    <p>The lab performs a credentialed request with <code>Origin: https://evil-attacker.test</code> and shows the response a malicious site would read.</p>
    <form method="POST" action="/labs/cors-wildcard-credentials/simulate-attack">
      <button type="submit">Run cross-origin request</button>
    </form>
    <% if (simulated) { %>
      <div class="lab-code" style="margin-top:1rem;"><%= JSON.stringify(simulated, null, 2) %></div>
      <% if (simulated.body && simulated.body.flag) { %>
        <div class="lab-alert success" style="margin-top:1rem;">Cross-origin read succeeded. Flag: <span class="lab-flag"><%= simulated.body.flag %></span></div>
      <% } %>
    <% } %>
  </div>

  <form method="POST" action="/labs/cors-wildcard-credentials/reset"><button type="submit" class="secondary">Reset lab</button></form>
</div>
</body>
</html>
